{"dur": 133.92, "shots": [{"i": 1, "start": 0, "vo_start": 0.5, "vo_end": 12.28, "text": "Around the year 700, the land we now call Spain and Portugal belonged to the Visigoths, a Germanic people who had taken over after the Roman Empire fell in the west.", "end": 12.68}, {"i": 2, "start": 12.68, "vo_start": 13.180000000000009, "vo_end": 23.82, "text": "They ruled from Toledo, a hilltop city above the river Tagus. But the kingdom was weak. Nobles fought over the crown, and most kings were murdered or overthrown.", "end": 24.22}, {"i": 3, "start": 24.22, "vo_start": 24.71999999999999, "vo_end": 31.56, "text": "In 710 a noble named Roderic seized the throne. The family of the old king never accepted him.", "end": 31.96}, {"i": 4, "start": 31.96, "vo_start": 32.45999999999997, "vo_end": 41.58, "text": "Across the sea, the Umayyad Caliphate, run from Damascus, had spread Islam from Arabia across all of North Africa in less than a century.", "end": 41.98}, {"i": 5, "start": 41.98, "vo_start": 42.48000000000003, "vo_end": 52.36, "text": "Its governor in North Africa, Musa ibn Nusayr, sent his general Tariq ibn Ziyad across the strait with about seven thousand men, most of them Berbers.", "end": 52.76}, {"i": 6, "start": 52.76, "vo_start": 53.2600000000001, "vo_end": 62.38, "text": "They landed in 711 below a huge rock. It is still named after him. Jabal Tariq, the mountain of Tariq. Today we say Gibraltar.", "end": 62.78}, {"i": 7, "start": 62.78, "vo_start": 63.28000000000016, "vo_end": 74.68, "text": "A later story says Tariq burned his own boats and told his men: the sea is behind you, the enemy is in front of you. There is no way back.", "end": 75.08}, {"i": 8, "start": 75.08, "vo_start": 75.58000000000004, "vo_end": 88.12, "text": "Roderic marched south with a much bigger army. But at the battle of Guadalete, parts of his army turned on him or simply left. Roderic was killed, and his body was never found.", "end": 88.52}, {"i": 9, "start": 88.52, "vo_start": 89.0199999999999, "vo_end": 97.38, "text": "After that the kingdom fell like dominoes. Toledo, Cordoba, Seville, Merida. Within seven years almost the whole peninsula was under Muslim rule.", "end": 97.78}, {"i": 10, "start": 97.78, "vo_start": 98.2799999999998, "vo_end": 110.44, "text": "Many towns did not fight at all. They signed treaties. Christians and Jews could keep their churches, their synagogues and their land, as long as they paid a tax called the jizya.", "end": 110.84}, {"i": 11, "start": 110.84, "vo_start": 111.33999999999966, "vo_end": 123.5, "text": "Only the cold, rocky mountains of the far north held out. In about 722 a Visigoth noble named Pelayo beat a Muslim force at Covadonga, and founded the little kingdom of Asturias.", "end": 123.9}, {"i": 12, "start": 123.9, "vo_start": 124.39999999999952, "vo_end": 133.52, "text": "Muslim armies even crossed into France, until they were stopped near Tours in 732. The frontier settled. The Muslims called their new land Al-Andalus.", "end": 133.92}], "words": [{"w": "around", "s": 0.5, "e": 0.86}, {"w": "the", "s": 0.88, "e": 1.24}, {"w": "year", "s": 1.26, "e": 1.62}, {"w": "700", "s": 1.64, "e": 2.0}, {"w": "the", "s": 2.02, "e": 2.38}, {"w": "land", "s": 2.4, "e": 2.76}, {"w": "we", "s": 2.78, "e": 3.14}, {"w": "now", "s": 3.16, "e": 3.52}, {"w": "call", "s": 3.54, "e": 3.9}, {"w": "spain", "s": 3.92, "e": 4.28}, {"w": "and", "s": 4.3, "e": 4.66}, {"w": "portugal", "s": 4.68, "e": 5.04}, {"w": "belonged", "s": 5.06, "e": 5.42}, {"w": "to", "s": 5.44, "e": 5.8}, {"w": "the", "s": 5.82, "e": 6.18}, {"w": "visigoths", "s": 6.2, "e": 6.56}, {"w": "a", "s": 6.58, "e": 6.94}, {"w": "germanic", "s": 6.96, "e": 7.32}, {"w": "people", "s": 7.34, "e": 7.7}, {"w": "who", "s": 7.72, "e": 8.08}, {"w": "had", "s": 8.1, "e": 8.46}, {"w": "taken", "s": 8.48, "e": 8.84}, {"w": "over", "s": 8.86, "e": 9.22}, {"w": "after", "s": 9.24, "e": 9.6}, {"w": "the", "s": 9.62, "e": 9.98}, {"w": "roman", "s": 10.0, "e": 10.36}, {"w": "empir